      "html": "<p>China: Changjiang River (Yangtze River).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amblycipitidae/liobagrus_marginatoides.htm",
      "html": "<p>The primary difference between Leiobagrus marginatus and Liobagrus marginatoides is that the posterior of the pectoral spine is serrated in L. marginatus.</p><p>Etymology: The specific name marginatoides: -oides, having the form of Liobagrus marginatus, to which it is compared.</p>"
